<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manuel Belgrano</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1770–1820</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manuel Belgrano was an Argentine economist, politician and general of the wars of independence. A member of the first junta of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> in 1810, he led an expedition to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paraguay">Paraguay</a> that was defeated in 1811. He created the blue and white flag of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a> in 1812 and won the battles of Tucumán and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salta">Salta</a> against royalist armies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manuel-belgrano.jpg" alt="Manuel Belgrano" width="320" height="388" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Attributed to Casimir Carbonnier · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Manuel_belgrano_by_carbonier_retouched.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
